&lt;h1 class="relative group"&gt;2023 was a rough year
 &lt;div id="2023-was-a-rough-year" class="anchor"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
 
 &lt;span
 class="absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none"&gt;
 &lt;a class="text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline" href="#2023-was-a-rough-year" aria-label="Anchor"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;
 &lt;/span&gt;
 
&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I usually enjoy doing these yearly posts,
looking back at what I did and planning what I&amp;rsquo;ll do,
but 2023 was a rough year.
I&amp;rsquo;m glad it&amp;rsquo;s over.&lt;/p&gt;</description><media:content xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="https://poolp.org/posts/2024-02-18/2023-a-retrospective./feature.png"/></item><item><title>I love you</title><link>https://poolp.org/posts/2023-03-01/i-love-you/</link><pubDate>Wed, 01 Mar 2023 12:00:00 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://poolp.org/posts/2023-03-01/i-love-you/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Almost four years ago,
your mom and I left home and rushed to the maternity hospital to give birth to your brother.
As I closed the door to our home,
I told your mom with a huge smile that the next time we&amp;rsquo;d open the door we&amp;rsquo;d no longer be only the two of us.
This was the best day of our lives.&lt;/p&gt;</description><media:content xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="https://poolp.org/posts/2023-03-01/i-love-you/feature.png"/></item><item><title>Farewell 2021, Welcome 2022: a personal post</title><link>https://poolp.org/posts/2021-12-30/farewell-2021-welcome-2022-a-personal-post/</link><pubDate>Thu, 30 Dec 2021 08:00:00 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://poolp.org/posts/2021-12-30/farewell-2021-welcome-2022-a-personal-post/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;
