&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As some of you know,
I was diagnosed a few years ago with &lt;a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Generalized_anxiety_disorder" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"&gt;generalized anxiety disorder&lt;/a&gt;,
&lt;a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Panic_disorder" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"&gt;panic disorder&lt;/a&gt; and
&lt;a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexithymia" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"&gt;alexithymia&lt;/a&gt;,
a trait that makes it particularly difficult for me to cope with the disorders.&lt;/p&gt;</description><media:content xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="https://poolp.org/posts/2021-08-13/august-2021-taking-a-break/feature.jpeg"/></item><item><title>Anxiety, OpenBSD break, COVID-19 and resuming work</title><link>https://poolp.org/posts/2020-03-30/anxiety-openbsd-break-covid-19-and-resuming-work/</link><pubDate>Mon, 30 Mar 2020 14:01:00 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://poolp.org/posts/2020-03-30/anxiety-openbsd-break-covid-19-and-resuming-work/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;
